1137	prey	7
owls hunt around they hunting territory away from where they roost during the day . they sit still on a perch , like a stump of branch , and wait for prey . they use they highly sensitive hearing to locate prey that can not be see . they use they very keen vision to see prey in the dark . they fly silently , without flap they wing , in order to surprise the prey . the owl silently glide or drop on its prey , grab it with its talon and beak . the owl eat the prey , or carry it back to its perch .
