667	carbon dioxide	8
solution cave be form in limestone and similar rock by the action of water . after a rain , water seep into crack and pore of soil and rock . the water percolate beneath the land surface . some of the water reach a zone where all the crack and pore in the rock be already fill with water . rainwater absorb some carbon dioxide as it pass through the atmosphere and even more as it drain through soil and decay vegetation . the water combine chemically with the carbon dioxide . a weak carbonic acid solution be form . this acid slowly dissolve calcite , form solution cavity , and excavate passageway .
