coal be load into the firebox . the boiler produce steam under high pressure . the steam generate in the boiler flow down into a cylinder . just ahead of the wheel , push a tight-fitting plunger , the piston . the piston be connect to one or more of the locomotive 's wheel through a kind of arm-elbow-shoulder joint call a crank and connect rod . as the piston push , the crank and connect rod turn the locomotive 's wheel and power the train along . a outlet valve open and the piston push the steam back through the cylinder and out up the locomotive 's chimney .
