bat and other animal produce a high-pitched tone . the sound travels in wave , as sound do . the sound `` bounce '' off of a nearby object . the sound wave return to the bat . the bat hear the echo sound . fold in the bat 's ear and adaptation in the bat 's brain enable it to determine the size , shape , and position of the other object via the property of the return sound wave . other animal use echolocation in generally similar way .
