air enter the nose or mouth and travel through the windpipe into the lung . the lung have a series of smaller and finer tube and sac . air reach the smallest and finest air sac call alveolus . oxygen travel from the alveolus into the blood . oxygen-rich blood be carry to the heart . oxygen-rich blood be pump throughout the body by the heart . cell take in the oxygen rich blood and release carbon dioxide rich blood . the carbon dioxide rich blood travels to the lung . carbon dioxide travel through the throat and be exhale .
